<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92283" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥεκ-τήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥέζω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>worker, doer</i>,
				like Homer's 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρηκτήρ, κακῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					191
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen.
			objecti, <i>worker in</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσοῖο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					1.297
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.149
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
